<title>USA: Clinton proposes some farm estate-tax relief.</title>
<headline>Clinton proposes some farm estate-tax relief.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Farmers would receive some estate tax relief under a proposal Thursday by President Clinton in his proposed fiscal 1997 budget.</p>
<p>&quot;The budget proposes to ease the burden of estate taxes on farms and other small businesses, allowing their owners to defer taxes on $2.5 million of value, up from the $1 million under current law,&quot; budget documents said.</p>
<p>&quot;The deferred taxes could be paid over 14 years at a favorable interest rate. In addition, the budget would expand the types of businesses eligible for such treatment by making the form of businesss organization irrelevant. It would also cut the administrative burden on taxpayers who elected deferral,&quot; the documents added.</p>
</text>
